privacy_main=r'''<main id="main">
<section class="subsite-hero corporate legal-hero"><div class="inner"><p class="subsite-label">01 / Privacy &amp; Cookies</p><p class="legal-kicker">CURRENT WEBSITE BEHAVIOR</p><h1>Website Privacy<br>&amp; Cookies Notice.</h1><p class="intro">This English notice describes the current website flows and contact routes. It is not presented as a formal KVKK Article 10 data-controller notice or as a privacy-compliance certification.</p><div class="legal-hero-links"><a class="button-link primary" href="#current-flows">Review current data flows</a><a class="button-link" href="legal.html">Website Legal Notice</a></div></div></section>
<section class="subsite-section paper legal-policy-section" id="current-flows"><div class="section-cap"><span class="num">02 / Current Website Data Flows</span><h2>The public site is informational and uses direct contact handoffs.</h2><p>The current website has no account-registration flow and no general server-backed contact form. Most routes present corporate, industrial, technology or portfolio information and link visitors to the relevant contact destination.</p></div><div class="legal-grid"><article class="legal-card"><span>BROWSING</span><h3>Public pages</h3><p>Visiting a public route causes the browser to request the page and its required assets. Ordinary connection/request metadata can therefore be handled by the network and hosting infrastructure that delivers the site.</p></article><article class="legal-card"><span>INDUSTRIAL RFQ</span><h3>Browser-prepared email</h3><p>The Industrial Sales builder accepts requirement and contact fields in the browser and prepares a mailto draft. The website does not send that RFQ to a server itself.</p></article><article class="legal-card"><span>DIRECT ROUTES</span><h3>Email and telephone</h3><p>Corporate and sales email links use mailto. Telephone links use tel. Following those links hands communication to the visitor’s chosen email or telephone service.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="subsite-section legal-policy-section" id="correspondence"><div class="section-cap"><span class="num">03 / Direct Business Correspondence</span><h2>Website handoff and business correspondence are different stages.</h2><p>A mailto or tel link does not by itself mean that the static website stored a submitted message. If you actually send an email, make a call or otherwise provide information through the selected communication service, that information can become business correspondence outside the static web page.</p></div><div class="legal-split"><div><span class="legal-label">WHAT YOU MAY CHOOSE TO SEND</span><p>Depending on the route and what you provide, correspondence may include your name, company or organization, email address, telephone number, commercial inquiry content, product/grade/quantity/destination/timing information, technical or specification information and additional notes.</p></div><div><span class="legal-label">LIMITED BUSINESS PURPOSES</span><p>Such correspondence may be used to respond to the communication, review an industrial requirement or continue the corporate, technology or venture discussion requested by the sender. This factual description is not a statement of a specific KVKK legal basis.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="subsite-section paper legal-policy-section" id="cookies-storage"><div class="section-cap"><span class="num">04 / Cookies / Browser Storage</span><h2>No website-set cookie or browser-storage item was observed in the reviewed flows.</h2><p>During the Phase 17 browser review of all 16 public routes on 1 September 2026, the current implementation did not set cookies in the reviewed flows and did not create localStorage keys, sessionStorage keys, IndexedDB databases or service-worker registrations. No analytics or advertising request and no page-script XHR, fetch or beacon call was observed.</p></div><div class="legal-callout"><strong>COOKIE-BANNER DECISION</strong><p>No non-essential cookie-choice banner was added because the reviewed implementation did not expose a non-essential cookie or similar tracking mechanism. This is a statement about the reviewed implementation, not a promise that the website can never change.</p></div></section>
<section class="subsite-section legal-policy-section" id="technical-delivery"><div class="section-cap"><span class="num">05 / Technical Delivery / External Requests</span><h2>Site delivery can involve ordinary request metadata and specific external image requests.</h2><p>Network and hosting infrastructure can receive ordinary information needed to deliver a web request, such as an IP address, browser/request information, the requested resource and request time. This notice does not state an exact infrastructure-provider role, log-retention period, processing location or transfer mechanism because those matters have not been source-locked for publication.</p></div><div class="legal-grid"><article class="legal-card"><span>EXTERNAL IMAGE HOST</span><h3>images.unsplash.com</h3><p>The reviewed current implementation requested externally hosted image files from <code>images.unsplash.com</code> on the Home, Energy &amp; Trade, Products and Industrial Sales routes. The Privacy and Legal routes do not request that external hero photography after this Phase 17 revision.</p></article><article class="legal-card"><span>NOT OBSERVED</span><h3>Third-party active code</h3><p>No third-party script, remote font, third-party embed, external media stream, analytics request, advertising request, XHR, fetch or beacon was observed in the reviewed website flows.</p></article><article class="legal-card"><span>EXTERNAL RESOURCE PRACTICES</span><h3>Host-specific handling</h3><p>When the browser directly requests an externally hosted image, the destination host receives the technical request needed to return that file and applies its own technical and privacy practices.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="subsite-section paper legal-policy-section" id="external-destinations"><div class="section-cap"><span class="num">06 / External Destinations</span><h2>External links become separate destinations when you choose to follow them.</h2><p>The website links to destinations such as the Evidence Axis specialist website/contact route and Google Maps. Those destinations are not presented as embedded services on this notice. Once followed, their operators apply their own content, technical and privacy practices.</p></div><div class="legal-link-row"><a href="https://evidenceaxis.com/contact/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Evidence Axis Contact ↗</a><a href="contact.html">Unique Holding Contact</a><a href="legal.html">Website Legal Notice</a></div></section>
<section class="subsite-section legal-policy-section" id="privacy-contact"><div class="section-cap"><span class="num">07 / Privacy Contact</span><h2>A current contact point, not an invented formal procedure.</h2><p>For a question about this website notice or information you previously sent in business correspondence, the current corporate contact point is below. Article 11 of Law No. 6698 provides data-subject rights where applicable; this page does not represent the address below as a separately verified formal rights-request procedure.</p></div><div class="legal-contact-panel"><div><span class="legal-label">CORPORATE CONTACT</span><a href="mailto:farahmand@uniqueholding.com.tr">farahmand@uniqueholding.com.tr</a><a href="tel:+902127272222">+90 212 727 22 22</a></div><div><span class="legal-label">RELATED ROUTES</span><a href="contact.html">Contact &amp; Business Routing</a><a href="legal.html">Website Legal Notice</a></div></div></section>
<section class="subsite-section alt legal-policy-section" id="legal-review-boundaries"><div class="section-cap"><span class="num">08 / Legal Review Boundaries / Last Updated</span><h2>Some formal privacy determinations remain outside this factual website notice.</h2><p>The site does not present a settled conclusion on the formal data-controller identity for all website/contact activities, the specific KVKK legal basis for each processing activity, recipient/transfer categories, retention rules or a formal Article 11 request procedure. Those matters require legal review before a formal Article 10 notice is represented as complete.</p></div><div class="legal-review-grid"><article><strong>FORMAL ARTICLE 10 NOTICE</strong><p>Legal review required before publication as a complete formal data-controller notice.</p></article><article><strong>TURKISH FORMAL NOTICE</strong><p>The public site is currently English-language. No machine-generated Turkish text is presented as an authoritative legally reviewed notice.</p></article><article><strong>LAST UPDATED</strong><p>1 September 2026</p></article></div></section>
</main>'''

